WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.055 --> 00:00:03.434
Ally held her breath.

2
00:00:03.435 --> 00:00:07.863
Julius' phone rang once, twice, then . . .

3
00:00:07.864 --> 00:00:10.176
"Hey, Mateo!" Julius said.

4
00:00:10.177 --> 00:00:14.592
"You reached me while I was reading a good spy novel. What's up?"

5
00:00:14.593 --> 00:00:18.762
"Uh . . ." Ally fumbled to read the script on Alpha's screen.

6
00:00:18.763 --> 00:00:24.438
"Hello, Julius. This is Allyzooba of Astralia, east of the Milky . . ."

7
00:00:24.439 --> 00:00:26.266
Her voice trailed off.

8
00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:30.831
"Eek! Alpha's script is terrible!" Ally thought.

9
00:00:30.832 --> 00:00:36.900
"Ally?" Julius sounded concerned. "Are you okay?"

10
00:00:36.901 --> 00:00:42.963
"I, er . . . I was wondering if you'd want to . . ." Ally flushed.

11
00:00:42.964 --> 00:00:45.227
"I mean you don't have to, no pressure.

12
00:00:45.228 --> 00:00:48.415
Oh, maybe this was a bad idea.

13
00:00:48.416 --> 00:00:51.095
I bet you were just being nice, right?"

14
00:00:51.096 --> 00:00:54.834
"Nice about what?" Julius asked.

15
00:00:54.835 --> 00:01:00.720
"About going on a date." Ally paused, and then added, "With me."

16
00:01:00.721 --> 00:01:03.086
There was a long silence.

17
00:01:03.087 --> 00:01:08.070
Ally started to sweat. "I knew it was a bad idea to ask you!"

18
00:01:08.071 --> 00:01:10.343
"Not at all!" Julius said.

19
00:01:10.344 --> 00:01:13.431
"I'm sorry, I just didn't know what to say.

20
00:01:13.432 --> 00:01:16.996
I've been trying to call you. But you haven't answered my calls.

21
00:01:16.997 --> 00:01:19.698
I thought you didn't want to talk to me."

22
00:01:19.699 --> 00:01:21.988
"Really? I . . ." Ally

23
00:01:21.989 --> 00:01:28.556
looked down at Alpha and guessed what had happened—Alpha still wasn't working right. "I'm

24
00:01:28.557 --> 00:01:31.204
sorry," she said. "My

25
00:01:31.205 --> 00:01:36.257
phone is, er, unreliable." "I

26
00:01:36.258 --> 00:01:38.803
understand," Julius said. "Anyway,

27
00:01:38.804 --> 00:01:41.573
I'd love to go a date with you." "You

28
00:01:41.574 --> 00:01:45.659
would?" Ally smiled. "That's great! Mateo

29
00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:51.135
suggested that we go on a double date to watch the eclipse on Saturday night." "That

30
00:01:51.136 --> 00:01:55.891
sounds cool," Julius said. "Should we meet in the park at seven?" "Yes!

31
00:01:55.892 --> 00:01:59.655
See you then!" Ally hung up the phone. She

32
00:01:59.656 --> 00:02:04.814
was so happy, she didn't even feel mad at Alpha for messing up the script. "Alpha,

33
00:02:04.815 --> 00:02:08.829
play some music. I want to dance!" "Harumph!"

34
00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:14.312
Alpha snorted and shut herself off. Ally

35
00:02:14.313 --> 00:02:19.528
shook her head. "Alpha's acting so weird," she thought. "Almost

36
00:02:19.529 --> 00:02:23.162
as if she doesn't like Julius or something. Hmm.

37
00:02:23.163 --> 00:02:29.412
Can computers get jealous?" ***

38
00:02:29.413 --> 00:02:34.984
The next day Ally was working at the counter while Flo was in the kitchen helping Randy.

39
00:02:34.985 --> 00:02:36.668
Barry rushed over.

40
00:02:36.669 --> 00:02:40.052
"I know what to serve for the food truck contest!

41
00:02:40.053 --> 00:02:43.161
I bet no one else will have it at their truck!"

42
00:02:43.162 --> 00:02:45.407
"What is it?" Ally said.

43
00:02:45.408 --> 00:02:48.316
"It's a surprise!" Barry said.

44
00:02:48.317 --> 00:02:50.944
"I'm going into the kitchen now to try it out."

45
00:02:50.945 --> 00:02:57.880
"I can't wait to see what it is," Ally said.

46
00:02:57.881 --> 00:03:01.715
Two customers came in and sat at the counter.

47
00:03:01.716 --> 00:03:06.734
"Can I get you something to drink?" Ally asked, handing them menus.

48
00:03:06.735 --> 00:03:09.452
"We're not here to eat," the man said.

49
00:03:09.453 --> 00:03:13.277
"I'm Jerry. I'm a producer at Food Truck Rally

50
00:03:13.278 --> 00:03:16.133
. This is Sally, my

51
00:03:16.134 --> 00:03:22.140
cameraperson." "Oh!" Ally smoothed her hair. "Am I on TV

52
00:03:22.141 --> 00:03:27.924
now?" "Not yet." Jerry laughed. "Is Barry

53
00:03:27.925 --> 00:03:29.612
here?" "He's in the

54
00:03:29.613 --> 00:03:33.569
kitchen. In fact, he's trying out a new recipe for the

55
00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:35.902
contest." "Oh, good," Jerry

56
00:03:35.903 --> 00:03:41.681
said. "We want to get footage of all the food truck teams in the days leading up to the

57
00:03:41.682 --> 00:03:46.155
contest. You contestants signed legal forms to participate in the

58
00:03:46.156 --> 00:03:48.885
contest. But we need everyone to fill out another

59
00:03:48.886 --> 00:03:51.487
form. Can you ask the others to come out of the

60
00:03:51.488 --> 00:03:55.864
kitchen?" "Sure! I'll get Barry, Randy, and

61
00:03:55.865 --> 00:04:00.220
Flo." Randy and Barry came out

62
00:04:00.221 --> 00:04:05.553
first. Jerry handed out sheets of paper. "Here are the waivers for you to

63
00:04:05.554 --> 00:04:09.411
sign." Ally, Randy, and Barry signed

64
00:04:09.412 --> 00:04:14.354
them. "Great!" Jerry said. "Now we can film

65
00:04:14.355 --> 00:04:18.085
you. Barry, can you tell the camera what you're working on?"

66
00:04:18.086 --> 00:04:24.137
"Well, I was going to keep it a surprise, but I suppose I can reveal it to the camera." Barry smiled.

67
00:04:24.138 --> 00:04:27.833
"I call it my Out of This World Cosmic Club.

68
00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:32.988
It's turkey and avocado, topped by huevos rancheros and potato chips."

69
00:04:32.989 --> 00:04:37.086
"That sounds like a winner to me!" Ally said.

70
00:04:37.087 --> 00:04:40.791
"What's a winner?" Flo asked as she came out of the kitchen.

71
00:04:40.792 --> 00:04:44.197
"Barry's sandwich for the contest," Ally said.

72
00:04:44.198 --> 00:04:49.352
"Here, Flo, you have to sign a waiver so the TV show can film you working."

73
00:04:49.353 --> 00:04:54.410
"Oh no!" Flo's cheeks flushed as she covered her face with a menu.

74
00:04:54.411 --> 00:04:56.829
"I don't want to be on TV!"

75
00:04:56.830 --> 00:04:59.266
"Really?" Ally was surprised.

76
00:04:59.267 --> 00:05:04.499
She thought everybody on Earth loved the idea of being on TV and becoming famous.

77
00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:07.281
"But you like to sing and make jokes and—"

78
00:05:07.282 --> 00:05:13.328
"I said no!" Flo scurried back into the kitchen with the menu still covering her face.

79
00:05:13.329 --> 00:05:17.756
"That was strange," Ally thought, confused.

80
00:05:17.757 --> 00:05:22.558
She tried to read Flo's mind, but she could only hear one thought from Flo:

81
00:05:22.559 --> 00:05:28.892
"Get me out of here as fast as possible!"

